{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkBF2Lg89ppuDes8QiYv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SUauYvjeM7zczYwb4amYUK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='src/view/sets.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"origin: [-3.3, 3.1, -1.6], pin: 'top'\",\"origin: [-7.6, 3.1, -3.4], pin: 'top'\")\ns=s.replace(\"new Precipitation({ kind: 'rain', count: 1400, area: [26, 12, 16] })\",\"new Precipitation({ kind: 'rain', count: 1200, area: [26, 12, 8] })\")\ns=s.replace(\"const center = new THREE.Vector3(0, 3, -3);\",\"const center = new THREE.Vector3(0, 3, -3.5);\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/content/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"export const TESTING_FEEDBACK\"); b=s.index(\"export const CREDITS\")\nnew='''export const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['HOW MANY ISSUES DID TESTING CATCH?', 'About 15 in the game: 5 from scripts (balance report and sim tests), about 10 from screenshots. Two more failures were bugs in the tests themselves.'],\n  ['HOW MANY WOULD BE CRITICAL OR GAME BREAKING?', '1: Op 4 could not be finished, because two bone fragments hid under pools that were already gone. The balance report found it.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE MOST HELPFUL TEST?', 'The whole game played by the bot in the real page on manual time: every scene, op and screen with the view running, in about a minute.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE LEAST HELPFUL TEST?', 'The rumble check: a stub pad only proves the call path runs, and no script can say how it feels. No person played this game, so feel and real-player difficulty are untested.'],\n];\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['WHAT DID YOU LIKE MOST ABOUT THE ENGINE?', 'Models as plain data plus the pixel pipeline. A 3D bust from a few boxes and slabs looks like a shipped game, with no art files.'],\n  ['DID YOU GET STUCK OR GUESS WRONG?', 'Rarely. wasPressed misses taps when a test presses and releases inside one slow software frame, so tests had to hold keys across frames. Palette-only model colours forced a material swap for skin tones.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE MOST IMPORTANT THING YOU HAD TO BUILD YOURSELF?', 'The painted tissue canvas: a per-frame 480x270 texture on a displaced mesh, which carries pools, wounds, stitches, gel and guides. Next, per-pad input with analog triggers.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE HARDEST PART ABOUT USING THE ENGINE?', 'Slow software WebGPU made browser tests timing-sensitive. Manual stepping with engine.step solved most of it.'],\n  ['WHAT DID YOU CHANGE IN THE ENGINE, AND WHY?', 'none'],\n  ['IF YOU COULD CHANGE ONE THING, WHAT WOULD IT BE?', 'Per-pad gamepad state with analog triggers built into Input, instead of one merged pad, so couch co-op needs no polling of its own.'],\n];\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['WHAT DID YOU LIKE MOST ABOUT THIS PROMPT?', 'The plan marks what was verified and gives working numbers, so I could trust them and spend the effort on the game.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS CONFUSING?', 'Very little. The title riff asks for the source name while the plan keeps every other use of it out, so I chose a title that riffs on the second opinion without repeating the name.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE HARDEST THING TO DO?', 'Judging hands-on feel and difficulty with no person playing: the bot proves each op can be cleared, not that it feels right.'],\n  ['WHAT WOULD YOU CHANGE IN THIS PROMPT?', 'Say how long a first-time human should take per op, so a bot-based balance report can be checked against something.'],\n];\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"Headless Node sim tests, Playwright Chromium browser tests with stub pads, hub harness runs, screenshots at 1080p\",\"Headless tools allowed, unlimited: Node sim and content tests, Playwright Chromium browser tests with stub pads, a bot playthrough of the whole game, five hub harness runs, screenshots at 1080p. No person played it\")\ns=s.replace(\"during the build I read the kit's guides and the hub README\",\"during the build I read the kit's guides and the hub README, and did no further research on the source\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"CONFUSING\\|lineH\" src/stages/about.js | head -3; node tools/build.mjs; timeout 300 node tests/run.mjs content 2>&1 | tail -14","description":"Fill About feedback, fix ward and rain, run content lint","timeout":310000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1819,"cache_read_input_tokens":476177,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1819},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"ea22e963-5a4c-46b2-b474-636e4e3e8992","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:30:08.917Z","request_id":"req_011CgkBF1vcsbGnBPADfsSPC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SUauYvjeM7zczYwb4amYUK":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='src/view/sets.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"origin: [-3.3, 3.1, -1.6], pin: 'top'\",\"origin: [-7.6, 3.1, -3.4], pin: 'top'\")\ns=s.replace(\"new Precipitation({ kind: 'rain', count: 1400, area: [26, 12, 16] })\",\"new Precipitation({ kind: 'rain', count: 1200, area: [26, 12, 8] })\")\ns=s.replace(\"const center = new THREE.Vector3(0, 3, -3);\",\"const center = new THREE.Vector3(0, 3, -3.5);\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/content/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"export const TESTING_FEEDBACK\"); b=s.index(\"export const CREDITS\")\nnew='''export const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['HOW MANY ISSUES DID TESTING CATCH?', 'About 15 in the game: 5 from scripts (balance report and sim tests), about 10 from screenshots. Two more failures were bugs in the tests themselves.'],\n  ['HOW MANY WOULD BE CRITICAL OR GAME BREAKING?', '1: Op 4 could not be finished, because two bone fragments hid under pools that were already gone. The balance report found it.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE MOST HELPFUL TEST?', 'The whole game played by the bot in the real page on manual time: every scene, op and screen with the view running, in about a minute.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE LEAST HELPFUL TEST?', 'The rumble check: a stub pad only proves the call path runs, and no script can say how it feels. No person played this game, so feel and real-player difficulty are untested.'],\n];\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['WHAT DID YOU LIKE MOST ABOUT THE ENGINE?', 'Models as plain data plus the pixel pipeline. A 3D bust from a few boxes and slabs looks like a shipped game, with no art files.'],\n  ['DID YOU GET STUCK OR GUESS WRONG?', 'Rarely. wasPressed misses taps when a test presses and releases inside one slow software frame, so tests had to hold keys across frames. Palette-only model colours forced a material swap for skin tones.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE MOST IMPORTANT THING YOU HAD TO BUILD YOURSELF?', 'The painted tissue canvas: a per-frame 480x270 texture on a displaced mesh, which carries pools, wounds, stitches, gel and guides. Next, per-pad input with analog triggers.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE HARDEST PART ABOUT USING THE ENGINE?', 'Slow software WebGPU made browser tests timing-sensitive. Manual stepping with engine.step solved most of it.'],\n  ['WHAT DID YOU CHANGE IN THE ENGINE, AND WHY?', 'none'],\n  ['IF YOU COULD CHANGE ONE THING, WHAT WOULD IT BE?', 'Per-pad gamepad state with analog triggers built into Input, instead of one merged pad, so couch co-op needs no polling of its own.'],\n];\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['WHAT DID YOU LIKE MOST ABOUT THIS PROMPT?', 'The plan marks what was verified and gives working numbers, so I could trust them and spend the effort on the game.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS CONFUSING?', 'Very little. The title riff asks for the source name while the plan keeps every other use of it out, so I chose a title that riffs on the second opinion without repeating the name.'],\n  ['WHAT WAS THE HARDEST THING TO DO?', 'Judging hands-on feel and difficulty with no person playing: the bot proves each op can be cleared, not that it feels right.'],\n  ['WHAT WOULD YOU CHANGE IN THIS PROMPT?', 'Say how long a first-time human should take per op, so a bot-based balance report can be checked against something.'],\n];\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"Headless Node sim tests, Playwright Chromium browser tests with stub pads, hub harness runs, screenshots at 1080p\",\"Headless tools allowed, unlimited: Node sim and content tests, Playwright Chromium browser tests with stub pads, a bot playthrough of the whole game, five hub harness runs, screenshots at 1080p. No person played it\")\ns=s.replace(\"during the build I read the kit's guides and the hub README\",\"during the build I read the kit's guides and the hub README, and did no further research on the source\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"CONFUSING\\|lineH\" src/stages/about.js | head -3; node tools/build.mjs; timeout 300 node tests/run.mjs content 2>&1 | tail -14","description":"Fill About feedback, fix ward and rain, run content lint","timeout":310000}}}
