{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkBXRKk6b5csSjfbxiUT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D8VxdGExvwtFYXZgPJmYA9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='src/content/models/index.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"{ name: 'cuff', cyl: [0.62, 0.62, 0.3], at: [0, 0, 0.54], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'fold' }, { name: 'wrist', cyl: [0.56, 1.6, 0.56], at: [0, 0, 1.46], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'glove' },\\n    { name: 'sleeve', cyl: [0.8, 2.6, 0.8], at: [0, 0, 3.4], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'sleeve' }] });\",\"{ name: 'cuff', cyl: [0.62, 0.3, 0.62], at: [0, 0, 0.54], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'fold' }, { name: 'wrist', cyl: [0.56, 0.9, 0.56], at: [0, 0, 1.1], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'glove' },\\n    { name: 'sleeve', cyl: [0.8, 1.3, 0.8], at: [0, 0, 2.2], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'sleeve' }] });\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/ui/hud.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"if (this.wheelT > 0) { // the big wheel, while picking\",\"if (this.wheelT > 0 && this.wheelSlot < 0) {\\n      const name = seat.tool.toUpperCase();\\n      hud.text(Math.round(W - size - hud.measure(name).width - 8), H - size - 4, name, { color: 0xffd24d });\\n    }\\n    if (this.wheelSlot >= 0) { // the big wheel, while the stick is pushed\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"wrist\" src/content/models/index.js | cut -c1-120 | head -2\ncat > ../exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-05 09:28:50\",\n    \"source\": \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Surgical action with visual-novel medical drama\",\n    \"perspective\": \"First-person surgeon's-eye close-up on a 3D operating field; talking-head close-ups and 3/4 room shots in story scenes\",\n    \"tech\": \"Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (riftlight kit: three.js r186, Rapier, WebGPU), own systems in JavaScript, esbuild 0.28.2, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's native low-poly 3D rendered as pixel art; procedural painted tissue canvases, original busts, tools, strains and sets; Kenney furniture recoloured for generic props\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's native rig clips on custom figures, SpringChain, LegStepper and Squash, plus procedural bust, tool, heartbeat and breathing animation\",\n    \"audio\": \"Everything synthesised in code: engine Song chiptune music (10% default), SoundDef effects, Animalese-style gibberish voices from pure-JS formant syllables\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 1 to 4 seats; couch co-op on its own with no network\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless tools allowed, unlimited: Node sim and content tests, Playwright Chromium browser tests with stub pads, a bot playthrough of the whole game, five hub harness runs, screenshots at 1080p. No person played it\",\n    \"research\": \"The plan's planner read the source's Wikipedia page, the hub's protocol and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes; during the build I read the kit's guides and the hub README, and did no further research on the source\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 16 in the game: 6 from scripts (balance report, sim tests and the sound lint, which found a misnamed wave making nine sounds and the choirs fail), about 10 from screenshots. Two more failures were bugs in the tests themselves.\",\n    \"1: Op 4 could not be finished, because two bone fragments hid under pools that were already gone. The balance report found it.\",\n    \"The whole game played by the bot in the real page on manual time: every scene, op and screen with the view running, in about a minute.\",\n    \"The rumble check: a stub pad only proves the call path runs, and no script can say how it feels. No person played this game, so feel and real-player difficulty are untested.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Models as plain data plus the pixel pipeline. A 3D bust from a few boxes and slabs looks like a shipped game, with no art files.\",\n    \"Rarely. wasPressed misses taps when a test presses and releases inside one slow software frame, so tests had to hold keys across frames. Palette-only model colours forced a material swap for skin tones.\",\n    \"The painted tissue canvas: a per-frame 480x270 texture on a displaced mesh, which carries pools, wounds, stitches, gel and guides. Next, per-pad input with analog triggers.\",\n    \"Slow software WebGPU made browser tests timing-sensitive. Manual stepping with engine.step solved most of it.\",\n    \"none\",\n    \"Per-pad gamepad state with analog triggers built into Input, instead of one merged pad, so couch co-op needs no polling of its own.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan marks what was verified and gives working numbers, so I could trust them and spend the effort on the game.\",\n    \"Very little. The title riff asks for the source name while the plan keeps every other use of it out, so I chose a title that riffs on the second opinion without repeating the name.\",\n    \"Judging hands-on feel and difficulty with no person playing: the bot proves each op can be cleared, not that it feels right.\",\n    \"Say how long a first-time human should take per op, so a bot-based balance report can be checked against something.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Second Stitch\",\n    \"tagline\": \"A surgical drama\",\n    \"description\": \"A melodramatic surgical action game in pixel art: ten operations against a clock, a terrifying nurse in your ear and a man-made disease called Mercy. Scrub in alone, or with up to four pairs of hands.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Simulation\",\n    \"source\": \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\",\n    \"series\": \"Trauma Center\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick or mouse moves the tool, R2 or left click uses it, right stick or 1-8 picks a tool, L2 or Space for your gift\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"pixel art\", \"story\", \"co-op\", \"boss fights\", \"comedy\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print('ok',len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']))\"\nnode tools/build.mjs; (timeout 590 node tests/run.mjs sim; timeout 280 node tests/run.mjs content) 2>&1 | tail -6","description":"Shorter sleeve, wheel only on stick, exit interview, run sim and content","timeout":880000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1824,"cache_read_input_tokens":483704,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1824},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"203420fc-4bc1-40d9-8203-688bb8f7fe56","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:33:54.478Z","request_id":"req_011CgkBXQ1cYff8g2cStHfEv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01D8VxdGExvwtFYXZgPJmYA9":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='src/content/models/index.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"{ name: 'cuff', cyl: [0.62, 0.62, 0.3], at: [0, 0, 0.54], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'fold' }, { name: 'wrist', cyl: [0.56, 1.6, 0.56], at: [0, 0, 1.46], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'glove' },\\n    { name: 'sleeve', cyl: [0.8, 2.6, 0.8], at: [0, 0, 3.4], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'sleeve' }] });\",\"{ name: 'cuff', cyl: [0.62, 0.3, 0.62], at: [0, 0, 0.54], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'fold' }, { name: 'wrist', cyl: [0.56, 0.9, 0.56], at: [0, 0, 1.1], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'glove' },\\n    { name: 'sleeve', cyl: [0.8, 1.3, 0.8], at: [0, 0, 2.2], rot: [90, 0, 0], c: 'sleeve' }] });\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/ui/h