{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C3dbZAVSJPWdKTd4sM2Yj4","type":"tool_result","content":"10://   node check.mjs --headless game.js    play the game in Node, no browser: steps, errors, a replay\n23://   --headless [game.js]             play a game module in Node with Engine.headless instead of a\n25://                                    the game its `createGame()` export returns, plays the --keys\n26://                                    frames, then replays that run's recording in a fresh game. It\n28://                                    1 on an error or a replay that ends somewhere else\n31:// It needs Node 20.15+ (or 22.2+) and, except for --headless, Playwright (`npm i -D playwright` then\n33:// `playwright-core` with CHROMIUM_PATH set to a Chromium (its headless shell,\n34:// `chrome-linux/headless_shell`, is the lightest): it plays WebGPU on SwiftShader with no\n56:const FLAG = new Set(['cameras', 'help', 'headless']);\n78:const headless = opts.headless === true;\n79:if (headless && (sheets || opts.cameras || opts.looks)) fail('--headless plays the game in Node, with no pictures: --sheets, --cameras and --looks need the browser');\n80:const target = positional[0] ?? (headless ? 'game.js' : 'index.html');\n207:// which the headless shell needs to present\n221: * --headless: the game in Node (Engine.headless), no browser. The engine is the pixel-engine.js the\n225:async function runHeadless(file) {\n227:  if (!/\\.m?js$/.test(path)) fail(`--headless plays a game module (game.js), not ${file}: pages need the browser (no --headless)`);\n231:  const report = { ok: false, mode: 'headless', module: relative(process.cwd(), path) || file, keys: opts.keys ?? '*90', frames: 0, fingerprint: null, replayed: null, status: null, state: null, errors: [] };\n233:    report.ok = report.errors.length === 0 && report.fingerprint !== null && report.replayed === report.fingerprint;\n236:    console.log(`check.mjs --headless ${report.module}: ${report.frames} frames in Node${report.status ? `, ${report.status}` : ''}`);\n237:    if (report.fingerprint === null) console.log('  not replayed: the run did not finish');\n238:    else console.log(`  fingerprint ${report.fingerprint}; replayed ${report.replayed === report.fingerprint ? 'to the same' : `to ${report.replayed ?? '-'} (not the same)`}`);\n243:  // a load, a setup or a replay that never settles fails, as a page that never starts does\n254:    const page = /\\b(document|window|location|localStorage|navigator)\\b is not defined/.test(msg) ? ' (code that touches the page runs only where there is one: guard it, export createGame(), GUIDE.md section 8)' : '';\n258:  const make = typeof mod.createGame === 'function' ? mod.createGame : null;\n259:  if (!make) fail(`${file} exports no createGame(): --headless makes the game with it, a fresh one for the replay (GUIDE.md section 8)`);\n266:    engine = await within(Engine.headless(make(), { assets: read, viewport: { width: vw, height: vh, dpr: 1 } }), 'the game\\'s start');\n276:    const rec = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(engine.recording()));\n277:    await within(engine.replay(rec, () => engine.loadGame(make())), 'the replay');\n278:    report.replayed = engine.fingerprint();\n292:if (headless) await runHeadless(target);\n298:    // headless (Playwright's headless launch is Chromium's headless shell): no display needed\n299:    return await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined, args: ARGS, headless: true });\n4606:### interface Recording\n4607-\n4608-- `readonly format: 1`\n4609-- `readonly engine: string`: The engine version that recorded it (a different one may not replay the same).\n4610-- `readonly game: string`: The game's name when it was recorded.\n4611-- `readonly args?: unknown`: What the game was made with (`Game.args`), when its name alone can't rebuild it.\n4612-- `readonly seed: number`: The engine seed (`ctx.random` comes from it and the game's name).\n4613-- `readonly time: number`: Game time when the level began (`ctx.time` carries on across levels).\n4614-- `readonly frames: readonly InputFrame[]`: Every frame the level ran, from its first.\n4615-- `readonly truncated?: boolean`: True when the level ran longer than a recording keeps (the frames are its start).\n4616-- `readonly from?: Snapshot`: The save-state the frames start from (`engine.restore()` began this recording), if any.\n4617-- `readonly view?: Viewport`: The viewport it was recorded on, as it was when the level began (CSS pixels and DPR): the art resolution, pointer aim and the HUD's layout follow it. A headless replay frames for it; a page warns when its own differs. A page \n4618-\n4619-### recordingProblem()\n4620-\n192:- `replay(rec: Recording, start: () => unknown, o: { frames?: number } = {}): Promise<void>`: Play a recording back: its seed and start time are restored, `start` loads the level it was made in (e.g. `() => engine.loadGame(new MyGame())`; it must not wait on frames, so load without a transition), then every frame runs with the recorded input, in manua…","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"4cc06c1b-c551-4a6b-8de5-38104daf232a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:41:32.603Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"10://   node check.mjs --headless game.js    play the game in Node, no browser: steps, errors, a replay\n23://   --headless [game.js]             play a game module in Node with Engine.headless instead of a\n25://                                    the game its `createGame()` export returns, plays the --keys\n26://                                    frames, then replays that run's recording in a fresh game. It\n28://                                    1 on an error or a replay that ends somewhere else\n31:// It needs Node 20.15+ (or 22.2+) and, except for --headless, Playwright (`npm i -D playwright` then\n33:// `playwright-core` with CHROMIUM_PATH set to a Chromium (its headle