{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkENtGaPNUNibxVVw15g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The Op 4 softlock is not open; it was fixed early in the build.** My line \"One is still critical\" was badly worded: it answered \"how many issues were critical\", but read as if the bug were still there.\n\n**The fix:** the two fragments were spawning under pools that had already been drained. They now spawn in the drain stage, under pools that still exist. The spawn code also clears `hiddenBy` if the entity hiding something is already gone, so this can't recur elsewhere.\n\n**Checked again just now on the current code, with the bot playing Op 4:**\n- **Full run at skill 0.7:** it won, finishing all 8 stages, and all six fragments were reachable when Bone Mend started.\n- **Balance report:** skill 0.4 gets B, 0.7 gets A and 1.0 gets S. Idle play still fails, as it should.\n\nThis is a bot check, so no person has played Op 4 either.\n\n**What changed:** only one line of feedback text, in the About screen and `exit-interview.json`. It now reads \"1, now fixed: Op 4 could not be finished…\".\n\n**After rebuilding with that text:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Content lint and sound | 375 passed |\n| Real stages in Node | 14 passed |\n| `check.mjs` on the page, with keys | passes |\n| `exit-interview.json` | parses |\n| Deliverable HTML | identical to the tested build |\n\nI didn't rerun the sim, browser and hub suites, because nothing but that text has changed since they passed (146, 57 and 5 of 5).\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1219,"cache_read_input_tokens":537161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1219},"output_toke