{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkGdQNCBvPDdtzpJzQo6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything in `PLAN.md` that can be done on this computer is done, and all suites pass on the shipped build. The one thing left is a human playthrough, which can't happen here: nobody has played the game, so hand feel and real difficulty remain unknown.\n\n## Your three points\n- **Suites not rerun:** all of them have now run on the final build, and the deliverable is byte-identical to the build they tested. After the last sim, content, hub and kit runs I changed only one test's wait; the browser suite was rerun with that change.\n- **Op 4 checked only by a bot:** a new test plays it through real mouse and keyboard events in the page. It picks tools with number keys, drains both pools, then grabs, turns and seats all six fragments, and the op moves on to the cement stage.\n- **Screenshot pass:** everything was recaptured at 1080p from this build: all arenas, all three Op 3 tables, all eight sets, the title, the results and HUD. The busts used in scenes are covered too, and I looked over the key screens.\n\n## A new bug the rerun found\nA pad check failed for the first time, and tracing it led to a real input bug. One-shot presses were being read in the wrong place:\n- **In a slow frame:** one press could act several times, so one Tab could skip a table.\n- **In a very fast frame:** a press could be lost.\n\nPresses are now read once per frame and passed to the next sim step, with tests at 15 and 240 fps. I didn't run those new tests against the old code, so they guard the fix but don't prove they would have caught the bug.\n\n## Final results\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Sim | 146 passed |\n| Content lint and sound | 375 passed |\n| Real stages in Node | 18 passed |\n| Browser, including the bot playing the whole game | 61 passed |\n| AI Hub harness | 5 of 5 |\n| `check.mjs` on the page, and `--headless` with keys | both exit 0 |\n\n## Limits of this testing\n- **Test changes:** two pad checks failed only on fixed waits under load, so they now wait on frames or a deadline. The flick and the R2 grab still have to happen for the checks to pass.\n- **Crashes:** several browser runs and screenshot captures hit \"Target crashed\" with about 3 GB free on this shared machine, which TASK.md attributes to memory. Reruns finished cleanly, and I retried those captures one screen at a time.\n- **Unused busts:** Ollie, Ottilie, Zamboni and Tomasz have busts, but no scene uses them. I checked those only as `check.mjs` model sheets, not in-game shots.\n\nI also updated the testing answer in About and `exit-interview.json` to about 21 issues, 8 from scripts and about 13 from screenshots. Nothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850/` (dev folder; screenshots are in `shots/`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2097,"cache_read_input_tokens":560854,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2097},"output_tokens":690,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"0b5f7974-688f-4f4f-b3cf-086e0122e77c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T18:40:32.177Z","request_id":"req_011CgkGdPveKue5tKRTxZ9MQ"}
