{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkJLVY15LCdzUrkagCFU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've closed the points from that feedback that can be closed here, and everything that can be done on this computer is done. A human playthrough is the one thing left, and it can't happen here: no person is available, and TASK.md lists what this machine can't do and says never to require it. Hand feel and real difficulty stay unknown until someone plays it.\n\n## Your points\n- **Frame-rate tests against the old code:** I temporarily put the old input path back, and 3 of the new tests failed. With the fix restored, all 18 pass, so they do catch the bug.\n- **The unused busts:** there were four, not three. Tomasz, Zamboni, Ollie and Ottilie each now have a line in their own scene. In-game shots confirm each one speaks and is visible, with no errors.\n- **Stability:** the browser suite passed three runs in a row on the final build, 61 of 61 each time, on a machine with about 3 GB free.\n\n## Results on the final build\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Sim | 146 passed |\n| Content lint and sound | 375 passed |\n| Real stages in Node | 18 passed |\n| Browser | 61 passed, three runs in a row |\n| AI Hub harness | 5 of 5 on the rerun |\n| `check.mjs` on the page, and `--headless` with keys | both pass |\n\nThe deliverable is byte-identical to the build these ran on, and no source has changed since.\n\n## Remaining doubts\n- **Hub stability:** one hub run crashed partway at 3 of 5, and the rerun passed 5 of 5. I expect it was memory, as in the earlier \"Target crashed\" runs, but my truncated output didn't keep the error line, so that's unconfirmed. Unlike the browser suite, the hub suite has only one clean pass on this build.\n- **Wrong-folder runs:** one batch of browser, hub and kit runs started in the wrong folder and failed to load. I discarded those and reran them, so none of the numbers above come from them.\n- **Loosened checks:** the two reworked pad checks still have to see the flick and the grab happen, but they no longer fail on a tight timing window. A pad bug that only appears under very low frame rates could get past them, though the Node frame-rate tests cover the keyboard side of that.\n- **Real hardware:** the controller, rumble and online play were tested with stubs and the hub's simulated network, not real devices. Sound was checked by rendering and play counts, not by listening.\n\nNo test can establish completeness beyond doubt, and I'm not claiming it. If someone plays this next, the first things to check are how the tools feel on a real DualSense and whether each op's difficulty is fair.\n\nNothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850/` (dev folder; screenshots are in `shots/`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_read_input_tokens":572905,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1161},"output_tokens":707,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"f4ca9b10-b6c9-4153-b911-f796fc668cfa","timestamp":"2026-11-05T19:02:56.032Z","request_id":"req_011CgkJLVDA726qz271x4Fe2"}
