{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkK98igEeotF5B9yBY4o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hub stability and the pad-check gap are now covered by test runs, and the shipped build hasn't changed. The one crash stays unexplained, and a human playthrough still can't be done here.\n\n- **Hub stability:** four more runs in a row passed 5 of 5, with 2.4 to 4.4 GB free before each. That makes five clean passes on this build. The one crash at 3 of 5 did not recur, but I never captured its error, so its cause stays unknown. It could be memory, as the earlier \"Target crashed\" runs were, or a rare fault I didn't catch.\n- **Loosened pad checks:** the gap I described is now tested. A new test drives the stub pad at forced 15 and 240 fps. One D-pad press moves one table, a flick picks the right tool, and R1 swaps back once. The browser suite is now 65 of 65.\n- **Human playthrough:** this can't be done on this computer, because no person is available. TASK.md says anything needing what the machine lacks is \"never required\", and the plan's testing section doesn't ask for one. More runs here won't change that, so hand feel and real difficulty stay unknown until someone plays it.\n\nThe deliverable is still byte-identical to the build all these runs tested, and no game source has changed since, only test files. `PROGRESS.md` has the final numbers, and nothing is committed to git.\n\nI consider this finished. The only open items are the unexplained crash and the playtest, and only you can arrange the playtest."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":578027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":825},"output_tokens":478,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_manag