{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkNsSqrecCugVDjWRjpU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The feedback was right: when I said \"done\" last time, it wasn't. This time I read the code against `PLAN.md` line by line instead of relying on the test list, and that found gaps no test had caught. They're all fixed now, and every suite passes on the shipped build. Nobody has played the game yet, so hand feel and real difficulty are still unknown.\n\n## What the audit found and fixed\n| Plan item | What was wrong | Now |\n|---|---|---|\n| §7: tool wheel for each seat | Only seat 1 had one | Other seats have one near their corner (tested) |\n| §7: tool icon by each tip | A text label | An icon (seen in the co-op screenshot) |\n| §9: gloves follow seat colour | Wrong colours | Red, blue, green, sand (seen in the co-op screenshot) |\n| §7: at most 3 awards per player | A lone player could get 4 | Capped (tested) |\n| §7: client corrects drift over 1 unit | Used 3 | Uses 1 (no dedicated test) |\n| §11: `?dev=` flag | Parsed, never used | Opens Dev Mode (tested) |\n| §12: live sliders | Aim Assist did nothing; Time Limit, Co-op Scale, Strain HP and Dies Irae BPM didn't reach a running op | All reach it (Time Limit and BPM tested, the Co-op Scale test only checks the stored setting, Aim Assist and Strain HP untested) |\n| §13: AnalyserNode check on a voice line | Never written | Reads a real level (tested) |\n\nTwo more turned up along the way:\n- **Hand and tool:** the hand never gripped the tool, because the arm and handle crossed. The palm now sits on the handle. I changed the plan's placement numbers for this, since it allows that if they can be beaten.\n- **Dish sound:** the dish \"tink\" used `Math.random`. It's gone, and no `Math.random` is left in the game's code.\n\n## The hub crash\nI can now explain it, though not prove it:\n- The crash was at the `page.evaluate` on line 16 of `hub.mjs`. That call only throws if the page has died.\n- The machine's `earlyoom` log shows it killing a `chrome-headless` process at 12:00:47, which fits when that run happened. Other agents' browsers get killed too, and I can't tie that process to my run.\n\nIt hasn't recurred in the ten hub runs since: 5 of 5 each time, one of them with only 1.9 GB free. So I put it down to memory on this shared machine, not the game.\n\n## Results on the shipped build\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Sim | 148 passed |\n| Content lint and sound | 375 passed |\n| Real stages in Node | 18 passed |\n| Browser | 71 of 71 |\n| AI Hub harness | 5 of 5, twice |\n| `check.mjs` on the page, and `--headless` with keys | both pass |\n\nThe build just before the sound one-liner also passed the browser suite twice and the hub three times. The 42 screenshots at 1080p came from that build too, since the one-liner changes no visuals. The deliverable is byte-identical to the tested build.\n\n## Still open\n- **Human playthrough:** this can't be done on this computer, and TASK.md says it's never required.\n- **The audit:** I did it by reading the code, so it found what I noticed. It reduces the risk of another gap but doesn't prove there are none.\n- **Real hardware:** the controller, rumble and online play have only been tested with stubs and the simulated network. Sound has only been checked by rendering, levels and play counts, not by listening.\n\nI updated the About screen and `exit-interview.json` to say about 29 issues, including the 8 from this audit. Nothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850/` (dev folder; screenshots are in `shots/`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2264,"cache_read_input_tokens":606994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2264},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"16bcc426-3634-4669-aaf8-e48de2b8ea1c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T20:02:27.819Z","request_id":"req_011CgkNsQHZdN8tXsuKxYUnG"}
