{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkPjdQ1Hs5UeFofLKfL2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Each gap you listed now has a test or a direct check, and all suites pass on the shipped build. The hub crash is explained as far as it can be without having caught that exact process.\n\n## Your list\n| Gap | Now |\n|---|---|\n| Client drift correction | Moved into a pure function and tested: left alone under 1 unit, eases toward the host above it |\n| Co-op Scale | Two seats drain vitals faster, live; alone it changes nothing |\n| Aim Assist | 60% speed near a target at Low, none at 0, and 50% damping across a stroke |\n| Strain HP | A running Introit and running eyes both change |\n| Other sliders | Every slider now has a behaviour test |\n| Seat wheels | Already tested; shown again on the final build |\n| Gloves and tip icons | Tested: gloves take the seat colour, and each tip has an icon |\n| §9 hand placement | The plan allows this (\"unless you can beat them\"), and a new test confirms the palm stays on the handle at all four corners of the field and the centre |\n\n## The hub crash\nI killed one of my own renderers, by PID, in the middle of a hub run. That produced the same error at the same line as the original crash: `page.evaluate: Target crashed` at `hub.mjs:16`. So that crash means a browser page died, not that the game failed a check.\n\n`earlyoom` killed a `chrome-headless` process at about the right time. I can't prove it was the same process, because the machine's other agents run browsers too. It's never happened in a run I didn't sabotage since: 13 clean hub passes.\n\n## Results on the shipped build\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Sim | 174 passed |\n| Content lint and sound | 375 passed |\n| Real stages in Node | 18 passed |\n| Browser | 75 of 75 |\n| AI Hub harness | 5 of 5, three times |\n| `check.mjs` on the page, and `--headless` with keys | both pass |\n\nThe deliverable is byte-identical to the build these ran on, and no source has changed since.\n\n## Still open\n- **Screenshots:** they came from the build just before this last change. That change only moved drift and slider logic into testable functions and touched nothing visual, so I didn't retake them.\n- **Browser suite:** it ran once on this exact build; the previous builds passed it repeatedly.\n- **Beyond this machine:** no person has played it, and real controllers, real online play and listening to the sound can't be done here. TASK.md says these are never required.\n\nI think this is as far as this computer can take it. The next useful step is someone playing it on a real DualSense. Nothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850/` (dev folder; screenshots are in `shots/`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1016,"cache_read_input_tokens":620759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1016},"output_tokens":710,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"cf18b318-66a5-4623-83ba-aef5ba82259c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T20:13:43.802Z","request_id":"req_011CgkPjd2vRaVnZN4eHi9pH"}
