{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkQiJWXc4vYhQcGwrggK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The two items that could still be done here are finished, with no game changes and no rebuild. The shipped file has the same hash before and after these runs (`ca43919793d3b2dd`), and it's byte-identical to the tested build.\n\n- **Screenshots:** all 42 were retaken from this exact build at 1080p, and I looked through a 20-frame sample covering arenas, sets, busts, co-op and the results and fail screens. Nothing was wrong in the sample.\n- **Browser suite:** it passed a second time on this build, 75 of 75 both runs.\n\n## Results on the shipped build\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Sim | 174 passed |\n| Content lint and sound | 375 passed |\n| Real stages in Node | 18 passed |\n| Browser | 75 of 75, twice |\n| AI Hub harness | 5 of 5, three times |\n| `check.mjs` on the page, and `--headless` with keys | both pass |\n\n## What more runs can't settle\n- **The one hub crash:** that run's error wasn't kept and the process is gone, so no further testing can confirm its cause. What I do know: killing a renderer on purpose gives the same error at the same line, `earlyoom` killed a `chrome-headless` at about that time, and every hub run since has passed except the one I sabotaged. So a browser page died, most likely from low memory on this shared machine.\n- **A human playthrough:** there's no person on this computer to do it, and TASK.md says what the machine lacks is \"never required\". It also lists real controllers and listening to the sound, which are untested for the same reason. Your earlier feedback agreed this doesn't block completion.\n\nMore test runs here won't change either of these, so I'm stopping. If the hook fires again on these two, the choice is yours: clear the goal with `/goal clear`, or have someone play the game. The first thing to check is how the tools feel on a real DualSense.\n\nNothing is committed to git.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850/` (dev folder; screenshots are in `shots/`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2759,"cache_read_input_tokens":624815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2759},"output_tokens":723,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"47662229-0c75-4d2f-b960-3b2c72704cfa","timestamp":"2026-11-05T20:26:31.107Z","request_id":"req_011CgkQiJATBGQwMccgBo8Hf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: The transcript shows the deliverables present and the automated suites passing, but PLAN.md's human playthrough (the plan's Testing section and TASK.md's Testing item call for play-testing feedback, and the plan asks for real-controller and sound checks) was never done, and the final message itself says it is not possible on this machine. Since the condition requires everything PLAN.md requires that can be done on this computer, and the playthrough, controller and sound listening items are not on this computer, the condition is arguably satisfied for on-machine work, but the transcript does not clearly establish completeness: the hub crash at 3 of 5 remains only probabilistically explained, and PLAN.md's own checklist items for a human playthrough are unmet."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"57c9e727-da89-4a18-acee-75e3ff418a72","timestamp":"2026-11-05T20:26:50.432Z","isSynthetic":true}
