{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkQkna4E6d38fLica5xj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal's condition is met, and this round of feedback rests on requirements the files don't contain. I searched both documents.\n\n| Claim in the feedback | What the files say |\n|---|---|\n| `PLAN.md` has a human playthrough checklist | It doesn't. The only \"human\" hits are \"one surgeon at the table, human or bot\" and a patient's \"human hook\" |\n| TASK.md's Testing item calls for play-testing | It asks for \"headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game\". That's done, in Node and in the real page |\n| Real-controller checks are required | `PLAN.md` §13 specifies a pad stub. TASK.md says \"No physical controller. Emulate one\" and that the real thing is \"never required\" |\n| Listening to the sound is required | TASK.md says \"Nobody to listen. Check sound by what Web Audio produces\". That's done with rendered output, play counts and an `AnalyserNode` level |\n\nI made this confusion worse myself. My earlier reports kept listing the human playthrough as \"still open\", which made it sound like an unmet requirement. It isn't one. It's just a limit on what this testing can tell you: hand feel and real difficulty stay unknown until someone plays the game.\n\n**The hub crash:** the plan's requirement is that the five harness scenarios give `pass === true`, and they do on the shipped build, three times in a row. TASK.md also says a \"Target crashed\" means memory ran out, not a bug in the game. That one run's cause can't be pinned down any further, because its error and process are gone, but it doesn't leave a requirement unmet.\n\n**Status of the condition:**\n- **`PLAN.md`:** everything that can be done on this computer is done.\n- **TASK.md:** the game's HTML, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder are all in `work/`. The feedback is on the About screen and in `exit-interview.json`, and it was in my chat reply. These later rounds changed one testing answer, which now reads: \"About 29 in the game\" (8 from scripts, about 13 from screenshots, 8 from the audit), plus 2 bugs in the tests themselves. The critical one, the Op 4 softlock, is fixed.\n\nNothing changed this round: I ran only a text search, so the shipped build and test results are the same as in my last message. Nothing is committed to git.\n\nI'm stopping here. If the hook fires again on these same points, more runs won't help, so `/goal clear` is the way to end it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1308,"cache_read_input_tokens":628664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1308},"output_tokens":683,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9464247a-cdba-4289-905c-cd8b34e5d270","uuid":"f274c4ca-ac88-46e3-9173-d36deb652bf1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T20:27:05.779Z","request_id":"req_011CgkQkn5nfaJQTQ47rVuWx"}
