{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkTwnm7kTSXKZEoDLdWc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm not doing any more work on this, because neither remaining objection can be settled from here. Nothing has changed since my last message: the shipped build and its results are the same.\n\n- **Independent verification:** you're right that the evidence is self-generated, since I wrote both the game and the checker. The only independent check I could start here is a subagent review, and TASK.md rules that out: \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" The hub harness and the kit's `check.mjs` are the only checks not written by me, and both pass. A truly independent verdict has to come from you or from someone you ask, and rerunning my own checks won't provide one.\n- **The hub crash:** it happened on an earlier build, and its error and process are gone, so more runs can't recover them. A dead page gives that exact error, as my deliberate kill showed, but that doesn't prove what killed the page. It has not recurred in any later run.\n\nMy view is that the condition is met, but that's my judgement and not an independent finding. If you want to verify it yourself, these are the quickest checks:\n\n1. **Play it:** open `SecondStitch-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-092850.html` and play Op 1 on a DualSense. This also covers what no test here could: how it feels and how hard it really is.\n2. **Rerun the tests:** the commands are in `PROGRESS.md`.\n3. **Check the evidence:** `docs/PLAN-CHECK.md` in the dev folder lists every requirement and what supports it, and the mapping is in `tests/plan-check.mjs`.\n\nTo end this loop, use `/goal clear`. Further hook messages on these same two points will get this same answer."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1358,"